  "query_preview": "..  (Tuesday through Next Sunday)\nIssued at 159 PM CDT Sun Jun 28 2026\n\nBy the start of the long-range forecast period Tuesday morning, \nguidance consensus is that the upper-level ridge will have amplified \nto its northern-most latitude across the eastern CONUS. While a \nmajority of global ensemble members have 850mb temperatures being at \ntheir warmest through this portion of the period on Tuesday, the \ngradual, subtle cooling through Saturday is expected to have an \nunnoticeable effect on surface temperatures thanks to the hot start to \nthe week. The main impact of these slightly cooler 850 mb \ntemperatures will be a more favorable thermal profile for air mass \nthunderstorms Thursday into Saturday. Given the brief, isolated \nnature of this potential convection, it is not expected to provide \nnotable heat relief. There is at least a medium chance that heat \nheadlines will be extended into Saturday, with the need for this \nbeing assessed with each forecast package. \n\nEnsemble clusters show the ridge retrograding westward for Sunday, \nwith deterministic guidance showing a shortwave passing through the \nMidwest. Both factors favor at least some degree of cooling through \nheight falls and/or a cold FROPA; however, specifics at this lead \ntime are highly uncertain. While ensemble spread in surface \ntemperatures increases on Sunday in response to this uncertainty, \nthe 25th percentile of high temperatures is in the upper 80s, \nsupporting a continuation of summer-like warmth.\n\nElmore",
